{"actor":"Erik Frèrejean","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T10:17:52Z","event_type":"updated","id":134,"issue_id":"weg-cw8.6","new_value":"{\"description\":\"Configure frontend linting tools: ESLint for TypeScript/JavaScript and Stylelint for SCSS. PHPStan is already configured (level max + Silverstan). PHP CodeSniffer rules TBD. ESLint and Stylelint config files do not exist yet — npm run lint:js and npm run lint:css fail.\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"weg-cw8.6\",\"title\":\"Configure linting and static analysis\",\"description\":\"Configure linting tools for both PHP and frontend code: PHP CodeSniffer for PHP style enforcement, ESLint for JavaScript/TypeScript, Stylelint for CSS/SCSS, and PHPStan for PHP static analysis. Each tool is configured with rules appropriate for the project.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"PHP CodeSniffer runs with SilverStripe-appropriate rules\\nESLint runs on TypeScript and JavaScript files\\nStylelint runs on SCSS files\\nPHPStan runs static analysis on PHP code\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":2,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"erik@wedevelop.nl\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-16T14:05:01Z\",\"created_by\":\"Erik Frèrejean\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-16T16:09:31Z\",\"work_type\":\"mutex\"}"}
{"actor":"Erik Frèrejean","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T10:17:53Z","event_type":"updated","id":135,"issue_id":"weg-ysw","new_value":"{\"notes\":\"Audit 2026-03-02: Core rendering and data layer complete (9 of 13 subtasks closed). Remaining 4 subtasks are interactive action UI: action callbacks (.2), add-element picker (.3), actions menu (.10), publish toggle (.11).\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"weg-ysw\",\"title\":\"Element Lifecycle \\u0026 UI\",\"description\":\"Content editors can create, publish, duplicate, and archive elements with clear status visibility, efficient navigation, and user-friendly error messages.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"Adding an element inside a Column shows only non-container element types\\nAdding a Row inside a Section shows only Row type\\nPublishing an element changes its status indicator from draft to published\\nModifying a published element shows \\\"modified\\\" status\\nClicking a content element nested 3 levels deep (Section \\u003e Row \\u003e Column \\u003e Content) navigates to the correct edit form\\nAn API failure during publish shows a toast message, not a blank screen\\nA rendering error in one element does not crash the entire grid UI\\nArchiving a Section shows a confirmation dialog before proceeding\\nDuplicating a Section creates a copy including all nested Rows, Columns, and content elements\\nArchiving a Row archives all its Columns and their contained elements\\nNo orphaned elements exist after any container operation\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"epic\",\"owner\":\"erik@wedevelop.nl\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-16T14:25:36Z\",\"created_by\":\"Erik Frèrejean\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-16T16:09:32Z\",\"work_type\":\"mutex\"}"}
{"actor":"Erik Frèrejean","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T10:17:54Z","event_type":"updated","id":136,"issue_id":"weg-q5d","new_value":"{\"notes\":\"Audit 2026-03-02: Backend GridConfigService (read-only config) exists. All subtasks (.1-.5, .7) still open — they cover the write/update path: grid update service, AJAX endpoints, CMS form fields, width/offset selectors, frontend API integration.\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"weg-q5d\",\"title\":\"Responsive Grid Configuration\",\"description\":\"Content editors can configure column widths, offsets, and visibility per viewport breakpoint, with changes saved immediately via AJAX.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"Setting a column to width 6 on a 12-column grid shows \\\"Half\\\" label\\nSetting width to 12 hides the offset selector\\nAttempting to set width 0 or 13 on a 12-column grid returns a validation error\\nAttempting to update grid settings on a non-Column element returns an error\\nAttempting to update without edit permission returns 403\\nGrid changes persist after page reload\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"epic\",\"owner\":\"erik@wedevelop.nl\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-16T14:21:28Z\",\"created_by\":\"Erik Frèrejean\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-16T16:09:32Z\",\"work_type\":\"mutex\"}"}
{"actor":"Erik Frèrejean","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T15:19:56Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":137,"issue_id":"weg-6c0.1","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"weg-6c0.1\",\"title\":\"Implement collapse state management with persistence\",\"description\":\"Create a state management system that tracks which containers are collapsed and persists this state across page reloads and CMS navigation. The state is keyed by element ID and stored in browser local storage. The system provides a React hook for components.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"Collapse state is stored per element ID\\nState persists after page reload (browser refresh)\\nState persists after CMS navigation (switching between pages)\\nComponents access collapse state via a React hook\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"erik@wedevelop.nl\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-16T14:30:37Z\",\"created_by\":\"Erik Frèrejean\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-16T16:09:31Z\",\"work_type\":\"mutex\"}"}
{"actor":"Erik Frèrejean","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T15:20:01Z","event_type":"status_changed","id":138,"issue_id":"weg-6c0.2","new_value":"{\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"weg-6c0.2\",\"title\":\"Integrate collapse toggle into container components\",\"description\":\"Add a collapse/expand toggle button to the Section, Row, and Column components. When collapsed, the container hides its children. The toggle uses the collapse state hook from E6.1.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"Section, Row, and Column components each have a collapse toggle\\nClicking the toggle hides/shows the container children\\nToggle icon indicates current state (collapsed or expanded)\\nToggle is keyboard accessible (focusable, activatable with Enter/Space)\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"erik@wedevelop.nl\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-16T14:30:50Z\",\"created_by\":\"Erik Frèrejean\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-16T16:09:31Z\",\"work_type\":\"mutex\"}"}
